## 1.0 Job Context

### 1.1 Overview of the Job Role

A part-time retail sales assistant is an employee who works for a retail business on a part-time basis and is responsible for assisting customers, promoting products and supporting daily store operations. Unlike full-time employees, part-time workers generally work fewer hours or specific shifts, depending on the employer's scheduling requirements. Despite having shorter working hours, they are expected to maintain the same level of professionalism, customer service and work quality as other retail employees.

According to the Ministry of Human Resources (2020), retail sales assistants are classified under Unit Group 5223 (Shop Sales Assistants) in the Malaysia Standard Classification of Occupations (MASCO). Their responsibilities include displaying merchandise, explaining product features, identifying customers' needs, recommending suitable products, providing price information and preparing sales receipts. These responsibilities demonstrate that retail sales assistants play an important role in ensuring smooth store operations and positive customer experiences.

### 1.2 Key Responsibilities

The main responsibility of a part-time retail sales assistant is to provide effective customer service while supporting the store's sales activities. This includes greeting customers, understanding their preferences, recommending suitable products and explaining product features and promotions. They may also be required to operate the point-of-sale (POS) system, process payments, handle customer enquiries and assist with product exchanges or returns.

Besides serving customers, retail sales assistants are responsible for replenishing stock, arranging merchandise displays, maintaining store cleanliness and ensuring products are properly organised. According to the U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics (n.d.), retail sales workers may also monitor inventory and maintain an organised working environment. Therefore, the role requires employees to balance customer service responsibilities with other operational duties.

### 1.3 Key Performance Challenges

Part-time retail sales assistants may encounter several challenges that affect their job performance. Firstly, **handling different customer behaviours** can be challenging, particularly when dealing with dissatisfied customers, complaints or customers who require additional assistance. Employees need effective communication and problem-solving skills to maintain customer satisfaction.

Secondly, **achieving sales targets while maintaining service quality** can be difficult. Retail assistants must understand product information, promotions and customer preferences to provide appropriate recommendations. O*NET OnLine (2026) identifies customer interaction, product recommendations and payment processing as important tasks within this occupation.

Thirdly, **managing multiple responsibilities within limited working hours** can affect productivity. Employees may need to serve customers, replenish shelves and maintain store cleanliness during the same shift. Additionally, retail work often involves standing for extended periods and working during busy periods, which may contribute to physical fatigue (U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics, n.d.).

Overall, the performance of a part-time retail sales assistant depends on their ability to provide quality customer service, achieve sales objectives, maintain operational efficiency and demonstrate professional behaviour.
